        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "bd6dfdf5-348b-559d-9bfe-e7c5d18abcda",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Levinson, William Link, Bruce Geller, Joe Mannix, Gail Fisher, Glenn Ford, Michael Cole, Loretta Swit, Peggy Fair\n- Works: Mannix\n- Roles: private investigator, secretary, executive producer, guest presenters\n- Awards: Golden Globe Awards, Emmy Award, Logie Awards of 1973\n\nFacts:\n- Bruce Geller was born on October 13, 1930, and he was an American lyricist, screenwriter, director, and television producer.\n- Mannix was created by Richard Levinson and William Link and developed by executive producer Bruce Geller.\n- In Mannix, Joe Mannix is the title character and he is a private investigator.\n- From 1968 through 1975, Gail Fisher played secretary Peggy Fair on the television detective series Mannix.\n- Gail Fisher won two Golden Globe Awards and an Emmy Award for playing Peggy Fair, and she was the first black woman to win either award.\n- At the Logie Awards of 1973, Glenn Ford, Michael Cole, Gail Fisher, and Loretta Swit attended as guest presenters.\n- Bruce Geller died on May 21, 1978.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2eec444d-d10f-52b9-aa0a-ae606bdad488",
        "text": "Page: Mannix. Sentence: Created by Richard Levinson and William Link and developed by executive producer Bruce Geller, the title character, Joe Mannix, is a private investigator.\nPage: Bruce Geller. Sentence: Bruce Bernard Geller (October 13, 1930 – May 21, 1978) was an American lyricist, screenwriter, director, and television producer.\nPage: Gail Fisher. Sentence: She was best known for playing the role of secretary Peggy Fair on the television detective series \"Mannix\" from 1968 through 1975, a role for which she won two Golden Globe Awards and an Emmy Award; she was the first black woman to win either award.\nPage: Logie Awards of 1973. Sentence: American film star Glenn Ford and television actors Michael Cole, Gail Fisher and Loretta Swit were in attendance as guest presenters.",
